<title>USA: U.S. weekend box office chart -- Feb 28-March 2.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekend box office chart -- Feb 28-March 2.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the February 28-March 2 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. The Empire</p>
<p>    Strikes Back	    $13,145,852	 $ 40,220,927</p>
<p>2. Donnie Brasco	    $11,660,216	 $  ----</p>
<p>3. Star Wars		  $ 6,856,626	 $125,081,792</p>
<p>4. Booty Call		 $ 6,429,364	 $  8,005,192</p>
<p>5. Absolute Power	   $ 5,728,082	 $ 36,863,422</p>
<p>6. Dante's Peak	     $ 5,268,165	 $ 52,335,485</p>
<p>7. Vegas Vacation	   $ 4,558,084	 $ 27,252,589</p>
<p>8. Fools Rush In	    $ 3,603,175	 $ 21,420,382</p>
<p>9. Marvins' Room	    $ 3,250,409	 $  5,380,309</p>
<p>10 Rosewood		   $ 2,909,767	 $  7,177,238</p>
<p>NOTE: Lifetime domestic gross for &quot;Star Wars&quot; is $447,821,934, and for &quot;The Empire Strikes Back&quot; is $262,895,193.</p>
<p>&quot;The Empire Strikes Back&quot; and &quot;Star Wars&quot; are released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;Donnie Brasco,&quot; &quot;Booty Call,&quot; &quot;Absolute Power&quot; and &quot;Fools Rush In&quot; are released by Sony Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;Dante's Peak&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;Vegas Vacation&quot; and &quot;Rosewood&quot; are released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;Marvin's Room&quot; is released by Miramax Films, a unit of Walt Disney Co.</p>
